ly tough for  kids to notice because it's somewhat  error appropriate to the film's  victorian sensibility  for example the everglads look down  their noses at victor van dorten as  family because  although they're wealthy their money  comes from running a canned fish empire  they dismissively call the vandorts fish  merchants and even though that's what  they actually  are it's implied that it's not a  respectable profession particularly  because a few hundred years ago  fishmonger was a euphemism for procurer  or a man who manages ladies of the night  on another occasion victor goes right up  to the edge of making a suggestive  gesture  while practicing his upcoming wedding  vows alone in the forest he gets a  little carried away with himself  with this hand i will cut your  oh goodness no by the time adults get to  the age where they're old enough to  watch corpse bride with their kids  they've absorbed volumes of cultural  history  most grown-ups can recognize references  and allusions to classic movies from  modern filmmakers who are cinema  devotees such as director tim burton  corp's bride is rife with nods to movies  as far back as the 1920s and 1930s  references the average child relatively  new to movie consumption probably  wouldn't be able to spot  in a scene in the lair of elder gut's  neck the character's hand passes by a  candlelit wall  it comprises only about a second of  screen time but it's enough to evoke a  famous shot from the pioneering 1922  vampire movie nosferatu  then in the big musical number remains  of the day the choreography of the  skeletons instantly brings to mind the  vintage creepiness of the bony dancers  from disney's 1929 animated short film  skeleton dance  the routine from corpse bride even  recreates the xylophone gag from the  original cartoon  which for some reason feels much more  disturbing than the modern version  burton also pays homage to his horror  master predecessor alfred hitchcock and  one of his most famous films  the group of crows that look down on  victor recalls the shot of the birds  looking down on tippy hedren's character  in the birds  corpse bride often alludes to the stars  of some of hollywood's most classic  films for example  alfred is an elegant and cultured  skeleton a denizen of the land of the  dead who strikes quite the handsome  figure in his purple jacket  and long thin mustache his living wife  gertrude doesn't recognize him without  his flesh but eventually she makes the  connection  you've been dead for 15 years frankly my  dear  i don't give a damn that's a reference  to the famous kiss offline from the 1939  classic gone with the wind  those timeless words were uttered to  scarlett o'hara by her former love rhett  butler  a character who like alfred sports a  very dapper mustache  one major character in corpse bride is a  full-on imitation of another movie star  of hollywood's golden age  although one who's been relatively  forgotten by the 21st century and  certainly not someone who kids would be  familiar with  in the film a maggot known only as  maggot lives inside the rotting but  living corpse of emily  their relationship is symbiotic in that  he presumably lives off her dead flesh  but also offers her friendship and  guidance  he's a charming and caring little guy  but his small talk could use some work  excuse me you don't know me but i used  to live  in your dead mother maggots is voiced by  anne reitel who delivers a convincing  vocal impersonation of actor peter  laurie co-star of classic films such as  m  the maltese falcon casablanca and  countless others  maggot even resembles the legendary  actor of course laurie might have had a  few  things to say about us comparing him to  a talking maggot  you imbecile you bloated idiot  you stupid father  corpse pride is an animated movie but  unlike traditional hand-drawn disney  movies or the computer-enabled  ultra-realistic pixar style it was  produced by the deliberate and extremely  taxing